WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:03.916
Hello, old friend.

00:00:03.916 --> 00:00:06.250
Ah, Ser Dwyane. Welcome to the Mediadel.

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:08.166
You’ll be reporting on an injury.

00:00:08.166 --> 00:00:11.875
Looks like the horse will be out...indefinitely.

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:14.000
I’ve seen that mark before.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.083
Yes. It's hand-checking, no?

00:00:16.083 --> 00:00:17.666
Since the horse's injury,

00:00:17.666 --> 00:00:20.833
my birds from Tor'Onto have become useless.

00:00:20.833 --> 00:00:23.041
They're just repeating the same things

00:00:23.041 --> 00:00:24.041
over and over.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:26.958
-Jordan is the GOAT!
-This generation's soft!

00:00:26.958 --> 00:00:27.958
Well, whatever it is...

00:00:27.958 --> 00:00:29.458
it seems to have spread.

00:00:29.958 --> 00:00:32.416
Dwyane, we've got to get to Cream City!

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.375
Giannis, come quick! We're being attacked...

00:01:03.583 --> 00:01:06.583
Welcome, everyone, to a very special edition

00:01:06.583 --> 00:01:08.333
of Inside the Realm.

00:01:10.875 --> 00:01:12.958
Dearest Maesters of the Mediadel.

00:01:12.958 --> 00:01:16.291
I now present the audition of Ser Dwyane Wade,

00:01:16.291 --> 00:01:18.958
for consideration of press credentials.

00:01:18.958 --> 00:01:23.041
Today, Ser Dwyane will be reporting on the horse’s injury.

00:01:23.333 --> 00:01:25.916
Dwyane, how will this affect House Raptors?

00:01:25.916 --> 00:01:28.208
It’s bad…it’s very bad, um…

00:01:28.208 --> 00:01:31.125
It’s a shame. He was their glue guy.

00:01:31.125 --> 00:01:32.750
Now more than ever.

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:34.916
Wait. I’m not done.

00:01:34.916 --> 00:01:36.625
The reason it’s bad is because

00:01:36.625 --> 00:01:39.375
Ser Jordan and the entire Dream Team are back

00:01:39.375 --> 00:01:43.916
and they’re going to destroy our Realm, one house at a time.

00:01:43.916 --> 00:01:45.541
What are you doing? Just wrap it up.

00:01:45.541 --> 00:01:49.166
Listen, no Jordan slander here, but he’s too old!

00:01:49.166 --> 00:01:51.666
Father Time is undefeated, aye?

00:01:51.666 --> 00:01:52.833
And let’s be real

00:01:52.833 --> 00:01:56.375
the only return Chuck’s making is to the buffet table.

00:01:56.375 --> 00:01:58.208
Yes, but that’s the thing.

00:01:58.208 --> 00:02:00.333
They’re all back in their primes.

00:02:00.333 --> 00:02:03.208
This is demonstrably preposterous!

00:02:03.208 --> 00:02:05.958
How could that possibly be conceivable?

00:02:05.958 --> 00:02:07.291
The Soul Box.

00:02:07.291 --> 00:02:09.541
Oh hooey!  My reporting showed

00:02:09.541 --> 00:02:11.625
that the Soul Box was smashed in Bostonia!

00:02:11.625 --> 00:02:14.833
Yeah, that was a top-19 moment in Bostonia basketball history

00:02:14.833 --> 00:02:16.250
and therefore basketball history.

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:18.833
The Soul Box’s power is not in the box,

00:02:18.833 --> 00:02:20.541
it’s in the shards.

00:02:20.541 --> 00:02:22.541
That was just a normal fart.

00:02:22.791 --> 00:02:24.625
No, the SHARDS.

00:02:24.625 --> 00:02:27.291
The fragments of the shattered Soul Box.

00:02:27.291 --> 00:02:29.166
They're made from the wood of

00:02:29.166 --> 00:02:32.083
Thou Maker's original peach baskets,

00:02:32.083 --> 00:02:34.291
Hickory Georgian Hardwood.

00:02:34.291 --> 00:02:36.250
H-G-H!

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:38.375
Ah, Jordan must have gotten the shards in

00:02:38.375 --> 00:02:41.083
the Terry Rozier trade. THAT’s why he paid so much.

00:02:41.083 --> 00:02:43.708
Oh hooey, Brian! I call shenanigans.

00:02:43.708 --> 00:02:44.791
Where’s your proof?

00:02:46.791 --> 00:02:49.416
Mama, there goes that man...

00:02:49.416 --> 00:02:50.000
horse.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.666
How’s THIS for evidence?

00:02:53.208 --> 00:02:55.500
-Is that Dan Majerle?
-I think it's Rex Chapman.

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:56.291
Who is that?

00:02:56.666 --> 00:02:57.958
That’s Wally Szczerbiak!

00:02:57.958 --> 00:02:58.916
No, it can’t be!

00:02:58.916 --> 00:02:59.666
Why not?

00:02:59.666 --> 00:03:01.250
Because I’m Wally Szczerbiak!

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:02.666
I think that’s Tom Gugliotta.

00:03:02.666 --> 00:03:05.458
No! I’m Tom Gugliotta.

00:03:05.458 --> 00:03:06.458
No you’re not.

00:03:06.458 --> 00:03:07.583
You’re Bobby Sura.

00:03:07.583 --> 00:03:09.583
Oh, right.

00:03:09.583 --> 00:03:10.541
It’s Christian Laettner.

00:03:10.583 --> 00:03:11.166
Bang!

00:03:11.166 --> 00:03:13.583
-OOOHHHHH, Christian Laettner.
-That’s right.
-He WAS on the Dream Team.

00:03:13.583 --> 00:03:15.291
So you’re telling me the Dream Team is back?!

00:03:15.291 --> 00:03:17.916
I don’t see the problem. This is the story of the century.

00:03:17.916 --> 00:03:20.583
Yes. But it would be the last story.

00:03:20.583 --> 00:03:22.916
Ser Jordan seeks to permanently end the debate,

00:03:22.916 --> 00:03:26.125
to prove he is the GOAT of GOATs.

00:03:26.125 --> 00:03:28.000
He’s coming for me.

00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:28.750
No, Paul.

00:03:29.083 --> 00:03:30.416
Truth. It’s the Truth.

00:03:30.416 --> 00:03:32.208
If anyone he’s coming for LeBron.

00:03:32.708 --> 00:03:33.708
Hey, that’s my bit!

00:03:33.708 --> 00:03:36.291
The people of every city he conquers are turned into

00:03:36.291 --> 00:03:39.541
mindless nostalgics with no passion for the modern game.

00:03:39.541 --> 00:03:41.291
Tor’Onto is already gone...

00:03:41.291 --> 00:03:42.041
-What?
-Noooo!

00:03:42.083 --> 00:03:43.416
As is Mill of Waukee...

00:03:44.083 --> 00:03:45.083
They're the best house in the Realm!

00:03:45.083 --> 00:03:47.000
Also, Detroit and Chicago.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:49.916
-Oh, OK.
-Well, that’s understandable.  
-I mean, Zach LaVine is pretty solid.

00:03:49.916 --> 00:03:50.583
No he’s not.

00:03:50.583 --> 00:03:52.541
We need to form a f--king wall!

00:03:52.541 --> 00:03:53.666
It’s no use.

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:56.333
There’s not a house in this Realm that can beat the Dream Team.

00:03:56.333 --> 00:03:59.291
You’re right. That’s why we’ve got to build one.

00:03:59.291 --> 00:04:01.458
Ladies and gentlemen of the Mediadel,

00:04:01.458 --> 00:04:03.541
we’re going to need your All-Realm ballots

00:04:03.541 --> 00:04:05.666
a little early this year.

00:04:08.041 --> 00:04:09.333
Thank you everyone for being here

00:04:09.333 --> 00:04:11.375
at this emergency Realm ‘All Hands.’

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.625
By now, you should all be familiar with

00:04:13.625 --> 00:04:14.958
the threat facing our Realm.

00:04:15.208 --> 00:04:17.208
So without further ado, I will announce

00:04:17.208 --> 00:04:18.916
the members of the Super Super House,

00:04:18.916 --> 00:04:21.416
hereby known as the Knights of the Round Ball,

00:04:21.416 --> 00:04:24.541
as selected by the Maesters of the Mediadel.

00:04:24.541 --> 00:04:26.041
Are you bloody serious? The Mediadel?

00:04:26.041 --> 00:04:27.583
-What do they know?
-Of course the Blog Boys pick...

00:04:27.583 --> 00:04:29.833
As president of the Knights Guild, I think this decision

00:04:29.833 --> 00:04:32.125
should be made by us, the knights of the Realm!

00:04:32.125 --> 00:04:33.125
HEAR! HEAR!

00:04:33.125 --> 00:04:36.000
I don’t know if that’s a... wise... idea.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.500
This is not the time of yore!

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:39.458
This is the era of knight empowerment.

00:04:39.458 --> 00:04:42.083
Let us vote, or we shan’t fight your battles.

00:04:42.083 --> 00:04:43.083
Yeah!

00:04:43.083 --> 00:04:47.166
OK, fine, but please take this seriously.

00:04:50.291 --> 00:04:53.375
OK, that’s another vote for Jamal Crawford.

00:04:53.375 --> 00:04:56.500
Oh Jesus Shuttlesworth…another vote for Melo.

00:04:56.500 --> 00:04:59.541
Another vote for Vince Carter, who’s 42. Cool.

00:04:59.541 --> 00:05:00.916
Actually I’m 43 now.

00:05:00.916 --> 00:05:03.250
Oh look. All three Plumlees!

00:05:03.583 --> 00:05:05.166
...and Jamal Crawford again.

00:05:05.458 --> 00:05:07.791
Look, if you're not going to take this seriously...

00:05:07.791 --> 00:05:09.041
I took it seriously.

00:05:09.541 --> 00:05:13.500
You voted for Allen Iverson. He cannot even play anymore.

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:15.583
How you gonna disrespect Iverson like that?

00:05:15.583 --> 00:05:17.750
One of you even voted for Michael Jordan.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:20.958
Hey, Ser Jordan was unstoppable in his prime.

00:05:20.958 --> 00:05:25.125
Yes, we know! That’s the whole point. We have to defeat him.

00:05:25.125 --> 00:05:26.125
Well, good luck with that.

00:05:26.125 --> 00:05:27.833
Maybe we should let the fanlings vote.

00:05:27.833 --> 00:05:28.833
Yeah!

00:05:28.833 --> 00:05:31.625
OK, listen...we experimented with letting the fanlings

00:05:31.625 --> 00:05:33.166
vote for the final roster spot...

00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:36.166
Let's just say it was a mistake.

00:05:36.166 --> 00:05:37.166
Well, who did they pick?

00:05:39.208 --> 00:05:40.125
Tacko Fall.

00:05:40.125 --> 00:05:40.791
Damnit!

00:05:40.791 --> 00:05:43.083
It’s OK, buddy. You’re still my little GOAT.

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:45.625
And while we all agree we love Tacko…

00:05:45.625 --> 00:05:47.250
we can also all agree...

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:50.750
we do not want Tacko defending the Realm against the Dream Team.

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:53.291
So you’re just gonna disrespect Tacko like that?

00:05:53.291 --> 00:05:54.291
Wow.

00:05:54.291 --> 00:05:57.625
OK, Tacko, do YOU want to go against the Dream Team?

00:05:57.625 --> 00:05:59.625
Uh, not particularly.

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:01.875
Right. Thank you. You may sit down.

00:06:01.875 --> 00:06:03.375
I am sitting down.

00:06:03.375 --> 00:06:06.458
Listen, this is not just any battle.

00:06:06.458 --> 00:06:09.958
If we lose, our fanlings will desert us,

00:06:09.958 --> 00:06:14.541
our economy will screech to a halt, and our society—

00:06:14.541 --> 00:06:17.750
which is solely based on interest in basketball—

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:19.958
will crumble around us.

00:06:19.958 --> 00:06:23.458
Before you know it, we will be on the verge of extinction,

00:06:23.458 --> 00:06:25.666
like the ice peoples of Hockeynia.

00:06:26.416 --> 00:06:29.958
So, here are the official Mediadel selections

00:06:29.958 --> 00:06:32.083
for the Knights of the Round Ball.

00:06:35.125 --> 00:06:36.125
King James,

00:06:36.583 --> 00:06:39.833
Ser Wardell Stephen Curry II,

00:06:40.166 --> 00:06:41.375
Ser Anthony Davis,

00:06:41.666 --> 00:06:43.416
Ser James Harden,

00:06:43.583 --> 00:06:45.208
Ser Kawhi Leonard,

00:06:45.208 --> 00:06:47.000
Ser Jayson Tatum,

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:48.666
Ser Rudy Gobert,

00:06:48.666 --> 00:06:50.458
Ser Luka Doncic,

00:06:50.458 --> 00:06:52.000
Ser Dame Lillard,

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:54.041
and Ser Joel Embiid.

00:06:54.041 --> 00:06:57.333
And replacements for the injured Kevin of Durant

00:06:57.333 --> 00:07:01.041
and the vanquished Giannis Antetokounmpo will be...

00:07:01.041 --> 00:07:02.250
Nikola Jokic

00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:04.958
Hey, yeah! House Nuggets! We did it!

00:07:04.958 --> 00:07:06.333
And finally,

00:07:06.333 --> 00:07:07.583
at point guard,

00:07:07.916 --> 00:07:11.666
the undersized and often controversial,

00:07:11.666 --> 00:07:13.208
but incredibly savvy…

00:07:13.541 --> 00:07:14.666
Ser Chris Paul.

00:07:14.666 --> 00:07:15.666
Are you kidding me?

00:07:15.666 --> 00:07:18.583
-Ridiculous!
-How dare you!
-Are you bloody serious? I'm an artist!

00:07:18.583 --> 00:07:19.583
I know, I know.

00:07:19.583 --> 00:07:23.041
Many of you are unhappy and feeling a sense of snubbery,

00:07:23.041 --> 00:07:24.666
but we must move on.

00:07:24.666 --> 00:07:28.541
So, where is this big battle supposed to take place?

00:07:28.541 --> 00:07:32.166
I say we go draw them into the mountains, the Denver Highlands.

00:07:32.166 --> 00:07:35.000
Denver? I think we should all fight for the Purple and Gold.

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:37.583
What better place for such a grand super house?

00:07:37.583 --> 00:07:40.625
I could never wear those colors. We should fight for Houston.

00:07:40.625 --> 00:07:43.041
No house better represents the modern game,

00:07:43.041 --> 00:07:45.333
the cutting edge of battle strategy.

00:07:45.333 --> 00:07:47.375
No, there’s no way that I’m doing that.

00:07:47.375 --> 00:07:50.000
We’re not going to any of those places.

00:07:50.541 --> 00:07:53.958
The location of the battle has already been chosen.

00:07:54.833 --> 00:07:59.166
It will take place at a house that everyone can agree on.

00:07:59.916 --> 00:08:02.500
A place where we can minimize collateral

00:08:02.833 --> 00:08:07.041
because the fanlings are sparse and already stuck in the past.

00:08:07.375 --> 00:08:09.541
A house with a history of defense.

00:08:10.166 --> 00:08:12.083
But most importantly,

00:08:12.083 --> 00:08:17.208
a place whose market viability I am interested in testing...

00:08:17.583 --> 00:08:19.875
Tonight, we ride…

00:08:20.666 --> 00:08:21.875
for Seattle.

